[{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/2671896386","html_url":"https://github.com/godotengine/godot/pull/103020#issuecomment-2671896386","issue_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/103020","id":2671896386,"node_id":"IC_kwDOAO6SJc6fQedC","user":{"login":"Nodragem","id":10520249,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjEwNTIwMjQ5","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/10520249?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/Nodragem","html_url":"https://github.com/Nodragem","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Nodragem/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Nodragem/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Nodragem/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Nodragem/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Nodragem/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Nodragem/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Nodragem/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Nodragem/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Nodragem/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"created_at":"2025-02-20T15:47:00Z","updated_at":"2025-02-20T15:56:16Z","body":"> That's a regression, they should be readded (I doubt they were intentionally removed, makes no sense UX-wise to not allow to rotate the other way). \r\n\r\nI never really used the CCW rotations, so I did not notice, but we can assign them to Shift + A, S, D or Alt + A, S, D.\r\n\r\n> with this PR rotating would still be affecting the selection. You'd need to additionally deselect (RMB) for the rotations to affect the to-be-drawn mesh. But this seems fine/acceptable to me.\r\n\r\nMight be a bit confusing. We could consider deselecting automatically then switching to Paint mode?\r\n\r\nAlso we need to test what happens when using the Move and Duplicate tool: we still want to be able to rotate a block of tile.\r\n\r\nEDIT: I just checked and this PR does not break the rotation during Move and Duplicate operations, so that's all good.","author_association":"CONTRIBUTOR","reactions":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/2671896386/reactions","total_count":0,"+1":0,"-1":0,"laugh":0,"hooray":0,"confused":0,"heart":0,"rocket":0,"eyes":0},"performed_via_github_app":null,"minimized":null},{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/2672433046","html_url":"https://github.com/godotengine/godot/pull/103020#issuecomment-2672433046","issue_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/103020","id":2672433046,"node_id":"IC_kwDOAO6SJc6fSheW","user":{"login":"kleonc","id":9283098,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjkyODMwOTg=","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/9283098?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/kleonc","html_url":"https://github.com/kleonc","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/kleonc/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/kleonc/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/kleonc/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/kleonc/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/kleonc/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/kleonc/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/kleonc/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/kleonc/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/kleonc/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"created_at":"2025-02-20T19:09:28Z","updated_at":"2025-02-20T19:09:28Z","body":"> I never really used the CCW rotations, so I did not notice, but we can assign them to Shift + A, S, D or Alt + A, S, D.\r\n\r\nI'm assuming there are some users who might be used to the previously available actions/shortcuts. They were previously <kbd>Shift + A/S/D</kbd> so makes sense to restore them exactly like that (only the shortcuts, no need for separate buttons). I see no reason to remove them.\r\n\r\nBTW the icons for the rotation buttons are confusing (2 of them show CCW rotation; they don't indicate the axis anyhow). But this can be tackled separately, at least it's clear they're for different rotations.\r\n\r\n> > with this PR rotating would still be affecting the selection. You'd need to additionally deselect (RMB) for the rotations to affect the to-be-drawn mesh. But this seems fine/acceptable to me.\r\n> \r\n> Might be a bit confusing. We could consider deselecting automatically then switching to Paint mode?\r\n> \r\n\r\nI'm not a GridMap user myself (but I can see the changes are definitely desired by the users, and I can check the code, hence did so), so I should be a good indicator of a newbie impression here. When testing I was initially surprised by it, so I'd say auto-deselect would make sense, yes. Is it the same for a regular GridMap user? You tell me. :slightly_smiling_face:\r\nAs already said current behavior seems acceptable to me. If it can be improved then go for it, sure.\r\n\r\n---\r\n\r\nAlso the current actions are named like \"Cursor Rotate X\", so it might need changing as well? Now it's not only for \"cursor rotate\", but also for \"selection rotate\". :thinking:\r\n","author_association":"MEMBER","reactions":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/2672433046/reactions","total_count":0,"+1":0,"-1":0,"laugh":0,"hooray":0,"confused":0,"heart":0,"rocket":0,"eyes":0},"performed_via_github_app":null,"minimized":null},{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/2673969289","html_url":"https://github.com/godotengine/godot/pull/103020#issuecomment-2673969289","issue_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/103020","id":2673969289,"node_id":"IC_kwDOAO6SJc6fYYiJ","user":{"login":"Nodragem","id":10520249,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjEwNTIwMjQ5","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/10520249?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/Nodragem","html_url":"https://github.com/Nodragem","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Nodragem/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Nodragem/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Nodragem/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Nodragem/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Nodragem/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Nodragem/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Nodragem/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Nodragem/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Nodragem/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"created_at":"2025-02-21T08:59:15Z","updated_at":"2025-02-21T08:59:15Z","body":"> BTW the icons for the rotation buttons are confusing (2 of them show CCW rotation; they don't indicate the axis anyhow). But this can be tackled separately, at least it's clear they're for different rotations.\r\n\r\nLet's open a proposal but maybe more generally about icons to be made/update. My guess is that many contributors are in the same situation as me: recycling existing icons, rather than using bespoke icons. Also, I think the tilemap editor does not use the brush icon for the paint mode; so we might want to discuss that as well.\r\n\r\n> Is it the same for a regular GridMap user? You tell me. \r\n\r\nIt is definitely an extra step, which can be confusing, to have to press ESC to deselect and rotate the brush. So if @Scarface1809 feels like adding an auto-deselect, it would be fab. I wonder if the selection can be \"saved\" and restored when the user goes back to selection mode? might be for another PR if not easy to do.","author_association":"CONTRIBUTOR","reactions":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/2673969289/reactions","total_count":0,"+1":0,"-1":0,"laugh":0,"hooray":0,"confused":0,"heart":0,"rocket":0,"eyes":0},"performed_via_github_app":null,"minimized":null},{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/2695215481","html_url":"https://github.com/godotengine/godot/pull/103020#issuecomment-2695215481","issue_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/103020","id":2695215481,"node_id":"IC_kwDOAO6SJc6gpbl5","user":{"login":"Scarface1809","id":118569321,"node_id":"U_kgDOBxE5aQ","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/118569321?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/Scarface1809","html_url":"https://github.com/Scarface1809","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Scarface1809/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Scarface1809/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Scarface1809/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Scarface1809/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Scarface1809/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Scarface1809/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Scarface1809/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Scarface1809/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Scarface1809/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"created_at":"2025-03-03T18:24:37Z","updated_at":"2025-03-03T18:24:37Z","body":"> It is definitely an extra step, which can be confusing, to have to press ESC to deselect and rotate the brush. So if @Scarface1809 feels like adding an auto-deselect, it would be fab. I wonder if the selection can be \"saved\" and restored when the user goes back to selection mode? might be for another PR if not easy to do.\r\n\r\nSounds good. I added the auto-deselect. As for saving the selection, I looked a little bit into reusing the existing last_selection variable (which is used for undo/redo), but I’m not sure if it would cause any issues. I think it’s best to handle that in another PR.","author_association":"CONTRIBUTOR","reactions":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/2695215481/reactions","total_count":0,"+1":0,"-1":0,"laugh":0,"hooray":0,"confused":0,"heart":0,"rocket":0,"eyes":0},"performed_via_github_app":null,"minimized":null},{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/2833553414","html_url":"https://github.com/godotengine/godot/pull/103020#issuecomment-2833553414","issue_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/103020","id":2833553414,"node_id":"IC_kwDOAO6SJc6o5JgG","user":{"login":"Mickeon","id":66727710,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjY2NzI3NzEw","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/66727710?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/Mickeon","html_url":"https://github.com/Mickeon","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Mickeon/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Mickeon/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Mickeon/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Mickeon/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Mickeon/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Mickeon/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Mickeon/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Mickeon/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Mickeon/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"created_at":"2025-04-27T17:11:41Z","updated_at":"2025-04-27T17:11:41Z","body":"What's this waiting for?","author_association":"MEMBER","reactions":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/2833553414/reactions","total_count":0,"+1":0,"-1":0,"laugh":0,"hooray":0,"confused":0,"heart":0,"rocket":0,"eyes":0},"performed_v